% Test cases for the oxygen policy (oxygen.le): synthetic claims, one or two
% per criterion of LCD L33797 and Policy Article A52514.
%
% DISCLAIMER. This program is an example of Logical English. It is provided
% "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including any
% warranty that it is accurate, complete, up to date or fit for a particular
% purpose. It is not an official reading of the Medicare texts it cites, it is
% not a coverage or payment decision of the Centers for Medicare & Medicaid
% Services (CMS) or of any Medicare contractor, and it is not medical, legal,
% billing or insurance advice. Its answers may be wrong: do not rely on them
% for a real claim, prescription or treatment; consult the official texts, the
% Medicare contractor and a qualified professional. Its authors accept no
% liability for any loss or damage arising from its use.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base oxygen cases includes these resources:
    oxygen.

the knowledge base oxygen cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete first-month concentrator claim: Group I at rest, the study by
% the treating practitioner, the order, the face-to-face (E1390 is on the
% required list since April 2026), delivery.
scenario group_1_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the concentrator.
    the HCPCS code of the concentrator is "E1390".
    the concentrator is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-05-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the arterial PO2 of Ann taken at rest is 54 mm Hg.
    the blood gas study of Ann was performed by treating practitioner.
    the treating practitioner ordered and evaluated the blood gas study of Ann.
    the blood gas study of Ann was performed at the time of need.
    the finding oxygen will improve the condition about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the treating practitioner examined Ann for the concentrator in a face-to-face encounter on 2026-04-20.
    the order for the concentrator is dated 2026-04-25.
    the order for the concentrator is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the concentrator includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the concentrator includes order date.
    the order for the concentrator includes description of the item.
    the order for the concentrator includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the concentrator includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the concentrator was communicated to the supplier on 2026-04-26.
    the concentrator was delivered on 2026-05-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the concentrator.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% A saturation of 90 at rest, nothing else: no group.
scenario not_hypoxemic is:
    claim 1 is for the concentrator.
    the HCPCS code of the concentrator is "E1390".
    the concentrator is furnished to Ben.
    the residence of Ben is private residence.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the oxygen saturation of Ben taken at rest is 90 percent.
    the blood gas study of Ben was performed by laboratory.
    the treating practitioner ordered and evaluated the blood gas study of Ben.
    the blood gas study of Ben was performed at the time of need.
    the finding oxygen will improve the condition about Ben is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].

% The study was performed by the DME supplier: not a qualifying study.
scenario supplier_study is:
    claim 1 is for the concentrator.
    the HCPCS code of the concentrator is "E1390".
    the concentrator is furnished to Cy.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the oxygen saturation of Cy taken at rest is 86 percent.
    the blood gas study of Cy was performed by DME supplier.
    the treating practitioner ordered and evaluated the blood gas study of Cy.
    the blood gas study of Cy was performed at the time of need.
    the finding oxygen will improve the condition about Cy is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers [].

% Group II: a saturation of 89 with cor pulmonale.
scenario group_2 is:
    claim 1 is for the concentrator.
    the HCPCS code of the concentrator is "E1390".
    the concentrator is furnished to Dee.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 2.
    the oxygen saturation of Dee taken at rest is 89 percent.
    the medical record of Dee documents cor pulmonale.
    the blood gas study of Dee was performed by hospital.
    the treating practitioner ordered and evaluated the blood gas study of Dee.
    the blood gas study of Dee was performed at the time of need.
    the finding oxygen will improve the condition about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% The same saturation without a Group II condition.
scenario group_2_no_condition is:
    claim 1 is for the concentrator.
    the HCPCS code of the concentrator is "E1390".
    the concentrator is furnished to Dee.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 2.
    the oxygen saturation of Dee taken at rest is 89 percent.
    the blood gas study of Dee was performed by hospital.
    the treating practitioner ordered and evaluated the blood gas study of Dee.
    the blood gas study of Dee was performed at the time of need.
    the finding oxygen will improve the condition about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers [].

% Group I during sleep only: the concentrator is covered, the portable
% system is not.
scenario sleep_only is:
    claim 1 is for the concentrator.
    the HCPCS code of the concentrator is "E1390".
    the concentrator is furnished to Eve.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    claim 2 is for the portable system.
    the HCPCS code of the portable system is "E0431".
    the portable system is furnished to Eve.
    the rental month of claim 2 is 1.
    the oxygen saturation of Eve taken at rest is 92 percent.
    the oxygen saturation of Eve taken during sleep is 85 percent.
    Eve is mobile within the home.
    the blood gas study of Eve was performed by independent diagnostic testing facility.
    the treating practitioner ordered and evaluated the blood gas study of Eve.
    the blood gas study of Eve was performed at the time of need.
    the finding oxygen will improve the condition about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Group I during exercise, with the three tests: both systems covered.
scenario exercise is:
    claim 1 is for the concentrator.
    the HCPCS code of the concentrator is "E1390".
    the concentrator is furnished to Fay.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    claim 2 is for the portable system.
    the HCPCS code of the portable system is "E0431".
    the portable system is furnished to Fay.
    the rental month of claim 2 is 1.
    the oxygen saturation of Fay taken at rest is 93 percent.
    the oxygen saturation of Fay taken during exercise is 86 percent.
    the three exercise oximetry tests of Fay were performed in one session.
    Fay is mobile within the home.
    the blood gas study of Fay was performed by treating practitioner.
    the treating practitioner ordered and evaluated the blood gas study of Fay.
    the blood gas study of Fay was performed at the time of need.
    the finding oxygen will improve the condition about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A fall of 7 percent during sleep with nocturnal restlessness: Group I.
scenario fall_during_sleep is:
    claim 1 is for the concentrator.
    the HCPCS code of the concentrator is "E1390".
    the concentrator is furnished to Gus.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the oxygen saturation of Gus fell 7 percent below baseline during sleep.
    the medical record of Gus documents nocturnal restlessness.
    the blood gas study of Gus was performed by independent diagnostic testing facility.
    the treating practitioner ordered and evaluated the blood gas study of Gus.
    the blood gas study of Gus was performed at the time of need.
    the finding oxygen will improve the condition about Gus is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Group III: normoxemic, cluster headaches.
scenario group_3 is:
    claim 1 is for the concentrator.
    the HCPCS code of the concentrator is "E1390".
    the concentrator is furnished to Hal.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the oxygen saturation of Hal taken at rest is 96 percent.
    the medical record of Hal documents cluster headaches.
    the blood gas study of Hal was performed by treating practitioner.
    the treating practitioner ordered and evaluated the blood gas study of Hal.
    the blood gas study of Hal was performed at the time of need.
    the finding oxygen will improve the condition about Hal is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A Group IV condition: a terminal illness not affecting breathing is a
% denial whatever else the record says.
scenario group_4 is:
    claim 1 is for the concentrator.
    the HCPCS code of the concentrator is "E1390".
    the concentrator is furnished to Ida.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the oxygen saturation of Ida taken at rest is 86 percent.
    the medical record of Ida documents terminal illness not affecting breathing.
    the blood gas study of Ida was performed by hospital.
    the treating practitioner ordered and evaluated the blood gas study of Ida.
    the blood gas study of Ida was performed at the time of need.
    the finding oxygen will improve the condition about Ida is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers [].

% Month 4 for a Group II beneficiary: the repeat study on day 75 and a new
% order; and the same claim without the repeat study.
scenario group_2_month_4 is:
    claim 1 is for the concentrator.
    the HCPCS code of the concentrator is "E1390".
    the concentrator is furnished to Dee.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-08-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 4.
    the concentrator was delivered on 2026-05-01.
    the oxygen saturation of Dee taken at rest is 89 percent.
    the medical record of Dee documents cor pulmonale.
    the blood gas study of Dee was performed by hospital.
    the treating practitioner ordered and evaluated the blood gas study of Dee.
    the blood gas study of Dee was performed at the time of need.
    the finding oxygen will improve the condition about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the repeat blood gas study of Dee was performed on 2026-07-15.
    the repeat oxygen saturation of Dee is 88 percent.
    a new order for the concentrator is dated 2026-07-20.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

scenario group_2_month_4_no_repeat is:
    claim 1 is for the concentrator.
    the HCPCS code of the concentrator is "E1390".
    the concentrator is furnished to Dee.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-08-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 4.
    the concentrator was delivered on 2026-05-01.
    the oxygen saturation of Dee taken at rest is 89 percent.
    the medical record of Dee documents cor pulmonale.
    the blood gas study of Dee was performed by hospital.
    the treating practitioner ordered and evaluated the blood gas study of Dee.
    the blood gas study of Dee was performed at the time of need.
    the finding oxygen will improve the condition about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers [].

