% A view (docs/user/reference/language.md §17.10): the reviewer's screen for an oxygen
% claim — the record by group, whether the claim is payable and, when it is
% not, the criteria it does not meet with their passages, the documentation
% that would be needed, and a letter for each outcome
% (/executive?program=lpsPlus/medicare/oxygen_cases&view=coverage desk).
the view coverage desk is:
    the title is "Oxygen coverage desk".
    the case is a scenario.
    the facts about "the claim" are
        a claim is for an item,
        the HCPCS code of an item is a code,
        an item is furnished to a beneficiary,
        the residence of a beneficiary is a place,
        the date of service of a claim is a date,
        the rental month of a claim is a number.
    the facts about "the qualifying test" are
        the arterial PO2 of a beneficiary taken a condition is a number mm Hg,
        the oxygen saturation of a beneficiary taken a condition is a number percent,
        the oxygen saturation of a beneficiary fell a number percent below baseline during sleep,
        the blood gas study of a beneficiary was performed by a performer,
        the blood gas study of a beneficiary was performed at the time of need,
        the treating practitioner ordered and evaluated the blood gas study of a beneficiary,
        the three exercise oximetry tests of a beneficiary were performed in one session,
        the medical record of a beneficiary documents a condition,
        a beneficiary is mobile within the home.
    the facts about "continued coverage" are
        the repeat blood gas study of a beneficiary was performed on a date,
        the repeat oxygen saturation of a beneficiary is a number percent,
        a new order for an item is dated a date,
        the medical record documents continued need for an item on a date,
        the record documents continued use of an item on a date.
    the facts about "the order and the delivery" are
        the treating practitioner examined a beneficiary for an item in a face-to-face encounter on a date,
        the order for an item is dated a date,
        the order for an item is signed by the treating practitioner,
        the order for an item includes an element,
        the order for an item was communicated to the supplier on a date,
        an item was delivered on a date,
        the supplier holds proof of delivery for an item.
    the judgments are
        the finding a finding about a beneficiary is an outcome.
    every fact shows who states it.
    the result is the answer to query pay.
    the result reads "Payable" when it holds.
    the result reads "Not payable" when it does not.
    the section applicability reads "Benefit category and scope".
    the section question reads "Coverage criteria (reasonable and necessary)".
    the section remedy reads "Conditions of payment".
    the result shows the stage it reaches.
    the result shows its reasons.
    the result shows its citations.
    the documents of the case are shown beside the facts.
    the result asks what is missing.
    the result can be flipped.
    the flip keeps
        a claim is for an item,
        the HCPCS code of an item is a code,
        an item is furnished to a beneficiary,
        the date of service of a claim is a date,
        the rental month of a claim is a number.
    the cases are listed with their results.
    the draft reads "DETERMINATION: payable.\nThe claim of {the case} was reviewed under LCD L33797 (Oxygen and Oxygen Equipment) and Policy Article A52514; it meets the coverage criteria and the conditions of payment.\n\nThe facts relied on:\n{the facts}\n\nThe passages applied:\n{the citations}" when it holds.
    the draft reads "DETERMINATION: not payable.\nThe claim of {the case} was reviewed under LCD L33797 (Oxygen and Oxygen Equipment) and Policy Article A52514. It does not meet:\n{the reasons}\n\nDocumentation that would be needed, if it exists:\n{the missing}\n\nThe facts relied on:\n{the facts}" when it does not.
